  "id": "site.kalev_smithy",
  "name": "Kalev's smithy",
  "name_1343": "Kalev's smithy (Schmiede, Lower Town craft quarter)",
  "landmark_id": "landmark.kalev_smithy",
  "confidence": "plausible composite: no Reval smithy plan of 1343 survives; plot from the modern footprint, form and layout after history/dossiers/architecture/smithy-workshop-layout.md",
  "sources": [
    "history/dossiers/architecture/smithy-workshop-layout.md",
    "history/dossiers/architecture/burgher-house-plan.md",
    "history/dossiers/crafts/blacksmith-materials-and-techniques.md"
  ],
  "period_notes": [
    "Stone-footed street-front craft house: the hot trade in limestone rubble (Hanseatic fire practice), forge bay ~55% of the ground floor behind the street door, living bay behind a stone partition (dossier decisions 1-3).",
    "Raised limestone-and-clay hearth under a clay hood against the east gable, venting through a rubble stack in the gable; bellows on the smith's left, anvil about 2.4 m down-fire, slack tub beside the anvil (dossier decisions 2 and 5).",
    "Charcoal in a roofed lean-to crib and a small corner bin, iron stock on a rack away from the quench, finished work on a fold-down shop counter at the street window (dossier decision 4).",
    "Not shown (dossier: do not show): trip-hammers, water power, brick chimney pots, glazed windows (wooden shutters only), a screw vice."
  ],
